    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0444" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330/7–1950: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-19T14:00:00+05:30">July 19, 1950—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 19—8:12 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. 1. Bajpai informs me not possible effect release messages so early as 9:30
                    July 19 Washington time because Nehru wishes his reply to Secretary’s message to
                    be delivered by Mme. Pandit today to be incorporated in release. Furthermore
                    Moscow must be informed.</p>
                <p>2. GOI is anxious that messages be published in New Delhi papers July 20 and
                    therefore is informing both Washington and Moscow its intention issue release
                    its exchanges with Washington and Moscow not including Nehru’s message of July
                    17, July 20, 3 a. m. Delhi time. I assume this permits sufficient time to elapse
                    after statement contemplated by President (Deptel 88, July 18).</p>
                <p>3. Fearing that there may be some delay in receipt reply by Mme. Pandit, Bajpai
                    gave me copy to transmit direct Department. If Mme. Pandit’s text not received
                    before time scheduled for release Department might arrange with her approval
                    publication text given me which is contained in Embtel 148.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d321-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henderson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d321-f1" n="1" xml:id="d321-f1-content">
                <p>Received at 9:27 a. m. on July 19, <ref target="#pg425">p. 425</ref>. The
                    Department of State released the texts of the Nehru–Acheson exchanges on July 19
                    at 3:30 p. m. (EDT); for texts, see the Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 19, 1950, p. 170.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
